Right's wide shot also shows more of the presenter, with the hands visible, and its captions sit at the bottom edge clear of the face. Left's captions overlap the hands and the lower body more.

Both have the same punch-in and the same card sliding in from the right. Both end on a clean lockup end card. Left's card shows green moving footage, which is a small plus. Right's card looks like dark text, so I can't tell from stills whether it moves. This doesn't outweigh the caption gap."}
